    "problem_statement": "# Chunked insert not working properly in dataset library\n\nHello,\n\nI've been using the dataset library for a while and recently noticed an issue with the chunked insert functionality. When using the chunked insert feature, data is not being properly inserted into the database.\n\n## Description\n\nI have a simple code that uses the chunked insert feature:\n\n```python\nwith table.chunked_insert() as chunker:\n    for item in data_to_insert:\n        chunker.insert(item)\n```\n\nThe problem is that when this code runs, none of the data is actually inserted into the database. The chunked insert operation seems to silently fail without any error messages.\n\nI've verified that the same data can be inserted successfully using the regular `insert()` method, so the issue appears to be specific to the chunked insert functionality.\n\nThe `chunked_insert_callback` method also exhibits the same behavior - the data is not being inserted and no callback is triggered.\n\nThis issue is causing data loss in our application as we're relying on the chunked insert feature for batch processing of large datasets.\n\nI believe this is a bug in the dataset library's chunked insert implementation."
  },
